#!/usr/bin/env -S uv run --quiet --script
# /// script
# requires-python = ">=3.11"
# dependencies = ["textual>=6", "websockets>=15"]
# ///
"""snitch - Little Snitch for Linux in the terminal.

Speaks the daemon's own web-UI protocol (ws://127.0.0.1:3031/stream): the same
process > host > address tree, the same rules. Blocking here is blocking there.

  up/down   move; the details follow     enter/right  open (expand)
  left      close / go to parent         x / space    block <-> unblock
  t, 1..5   time window                  /            search, esc clears
  s         sort by activity, re-sorted every 10s (s again: 20s)
  S         sort by name                 e            egress graph (sender -> destination)
  q         quit

Subcommands (default: the overview above):
  snitch egress            start in the egress graph
  snitch watch             alert popups for connections denied by default (user service)
  snitch ask FILE          one popup: o allow, x block, O / X for `temporary`, esc later
  snitch status            waybar JSON
  snitch default deny      try deny by default (baseline first): goes back to allow by itself after
                           `trial` (10m), and at the next boot, unless confirmed with --keep
  snitch default allow     back to allow by default
  snitch baseline          allow rules a deny-by-default box needs (RDP, DNS, DHCP, NTP, apt)
  snitch baseline --dev    plus the dev tools, each to its own hosts only (Claude, Codex, gh, git,
                           npm, uv, pip, cargo, go, podman): for jobs that run while you're away

Config ~/.config/snitch/config.toml (all optional):
  periods = ["15m", "30m", "1h", "24h", "7d"]
  since   = "1h"
  protect = ["hypr-rdp", "sshd"]   # blocking these asks for a second x
  resort  = [10, 20]               # seconds between activity re-sorts, s cycles
  temporary = "15m"                # O / X in the popup
  snooze  = "10m"                  # esc in the popup: ask again after this
  trial   = "10m"                  # snitch default deny: back to allow after this unless --keep
Log of blocks / unblocks and blocked connections: ~/.local/state/snitch/snitch.log
"""
